        "original_id": "3c01655a-dddb-560a-8e6d-431adf28c6e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mervyn Peake, Robert Erskine Childers, Gretchen Osgood Warren, Hamilton Osgood, Margaret Cushing Osgood, Mary Alden Childers\n- Works: Gormenghast books, The Riddle of the Sands, Titus Alone\n- Places: Beacon Hill, Boston, Massachusetts, Ireland\n- Objects: Asgard\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Erskine Childers was born on 25 June 1870 and died on 24 November 1922.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was a British writer whose works included the influential novel The Riddle of the Sands.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was also a Fenian revolutionary who smuggled guns to Ireland in his sailing yacht Asgard.\n- Titus Alone is a novel by Mervyn Peake that was first published in 1959.\n- Mervyn Peake is best known for what are usually referred to as the Gormenghast books.\n- Gretchen Osgood Warren was the daughter of Dr. Hamilton Osgood and Margaret Cushing Osgood of Beacon Hill, Boston, Massachusetts.\n- Mary Alden Childers was the younger sister of Gretchen Osgood Warren and the wife of writer and Irish nationalist Robert Erskine Childers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d4c99114-f823-530e-a779-8736926647f4",
